===== 3. boundary-call counts (counting build) =====
# boundary-call counts, arm core-ffi-rust
#   counting build: YES
#   guard:          on

payload direction  elements   strings   forward   reverse  crossings  transc  prefix
P1.1    enc cold          4        20         2         1          3      24       1
P1.1    enc warm          4        20         2         1          3      24       0
P1.1    decode            4        20         1         2          3       0       0
P1.2    enc cold       1000      5000         8         1          9    6000       1
P1.2    enc warm       1000      5000         8         1          9    6000       0
P1.2    decode         1000      5000         1         5          6       0       0
P1.3    enc cold        300         0         3         1          4       0       0
P1.3    enc warm        300         0         3         1          4       0       0
P1.3    decode          300         0         1         3          4       0       0

# `crossings` is forward + reverse: calls that leave one side's compilation unit.
# `transc` counts transcoder invocations, which are indirect calls the core makes
#   into ITSELF (ABI v1 section 4 puts every representation in the core), so they
#   are not host crossings. Counting them together is what made the drafted
#   interface look like 15,137 calls on a 1,000-row response.
# `prefix` counts length-placeholder resizes, in the steady state: ABI v1 open
#   decision 5.

===== 4. the boundary is real =====
